{"kind":"propose","text":"Adopt the intersection rule for promise scope: a promise kind-definition carries an optional conditions field mirroring the request form; when present, the promise visibly narrows the request and the effective conditions of satisfaction become the intersection - what was asked, as narrowed by what was undertaken. The projection surfaces the narrowing at promise time so the requester can dissent then rather than at report time; ratification of the report is the requester accepting the narrowed scope on the record. No new verbs or kinds; no fold change before the starter definitions land byte-for-byte - this amends the promise definition by ordinary supersession afterward. Rationale: mismatch between request and promise is normal cooperation, not error; recording the intersection is the honest form (Promise Theory alignment, assert 19d40ded)."}